1. ऋष् cl. 1. P. अर्षति, आनर्ष, अर्षिता, to flow, flow quickly, glide, move with a quick motion, RV.; AV.; VS.;
to bring near by flowing, RV.;
 [cf. Gk. ἔρση (?); ἄψ-ορρος, ‘flowing back’; παλίν-ορσος, ‘darting back’.]

2. ऋष् cl. 6. P. ऋषति, आनर्ष, अर्षिता, to go, move, Dhātup. xxviii, 7;
to stab, kill, AV. ix, 4, 17;
to push, thrust.
